        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## 05 — Plate upres, both paths\n\nTake the 480p generated section back up to plate resolution without it looking AI-smeared.\nGenerative work happens at model resolution; delivery does not.\n\n**esrgan** — RealESRGAN_x4plus, fixed 4x, then a lanczos fit to 1920x1080. Deterministic: same\ninput, same pixels, no invented detail. This is the one a comp supervisor signs off.\n\n**seedvr2** — resize to 1920x1080, then SeedVR2 3B int8 restores at that resolution in one step\n(denoise 1, cfg 1, euler/simple). It *does* invent detail — that is the point when the source is\nsoft, and the reason it needs a look before it ships.\n\nModels: `seedvr2_3b_int8_convrot.safetensors` (3.22 GB, diffusion_models) and\n`seedvr2_ema_vae_fp16.safetensors` (0.47 GB, vae), both Apache-2.0;\n`RealESRGAN_x4plus.safetensors` (0.06 GB, upscale_models), BSD-3.\n\nDerived from the core templates `utility-gan_upscaler` and `utility_seedvr2_3b_int8_upscale_image`\n(Comfy-Org/workflow_templates, MIT), with the SeedVR2 subgraph expanded to plain nodes so the\nsampler is visible to provenance.\n\nDeliberately **not** SUPIR: `utility_image_upscale_supir` is a nicer restorer and its weights are\nnon-commercial, so it cannot ship in a studio delivery."
      ],
      "title": "Note"
    },
